orgia,serif;margin:0 0 10px"><span>Unlikely power players</span></h2><p sty=
le=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span=
 style=3D"font-weight:700">Vivian, give me the 101 version: Who are the Hou=
this=3F</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#33=
3;margin:0 0 15px"><span>In the early 2000s, they were this ragtag militia =
in northern Yemen =E2=80=94 rebels with guns who were fighting the central =
government. But over the past decade or so, they=E2=80=99ve become these un=
likely power players in the region. They fought a Saudi-led military coalit=
ion to a quasi-draw in Yemen=E2=80=99s civil war. They became a headache fo=
r the United States and the rest of the world when they started attacking s=
hipping in the Red Sea in 2023. They=E2=80=99ve also become more sophistica=
ted. A recent report from Anthropic had a section suggesting they tried to =
use Claude to design guidance systems for rockets. People all over the worl=
d are kind of fascinated by them.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25=
px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The Houthis lord over a =
repressive de facto state that provides limited services to its impoverishe=
d people. They can be incredibly brutal. They believe they have a divine ma=
ndate to rule. Their slogan calls for death to America and Israel and =E2=
=80=9Ca curse upon the Jews.=E2=80=9D</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17p=
x/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>But they=E2=80=99re =
also these underdogs who have consistently defied expectations. Time and ti=
me again, they=E2=80=99ve gone up against much bigger, wealthier foes. And =
time and again, those foes have been forced to back down.</span></p><table =
