e=3D"font-weight:700">When we talk about the Houthis, we always call them a=
n =E2=80=9CIranian-backed militia.=E2=80=9D How does Iran fit in here=3F</s=
pan></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0=
 0 15px"><span>The Houthis get support and weaponry from Iran and have been=
 important allies. And their current ability to disrupt shipping in the Red=
 Sea and the Bab al-Mandab Strait is giving Iran extra leverage in its war =
at a crucial time. But it=E2=80=99s important to understand that they=E2=80=
=99re doing this for themselves as much as they=E2=80=99re doing it for Ira=
n. They very much have their own goals.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 1=
7px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-weig=
ht:700">Which are=3F</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,se=
rif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The Houthis describe themselves as th=
e liberators and legitimate leaders of Yemen. That pits them against the Sa=
udi-backed government. The Houthis say they want the Saudis out, by which t=
hey mean they want the Saudis to stop supporting their Yemeni foes. They al=
so want money, like access to Yemeni oil revenue and war reparations from S=
audi Arabia, among other things. And they=E2=80=99re picking this moment to=
 make a big push.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif=
;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-weight:700">Let=E2=80=99s =
step back. Who actually governs Yemen=3F</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal =
17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>It=E2=80=99s comp=
licated. There=E2=80=99s an internationally recognized Yemeni government, b=
ut a lot of people call them a quote-unquote =E2=80=9Cgovernment.=E2=80=9D =
At this point, the government is effectively a bunch of armed groups and ot=
her entities, under a council of eight different men.</span></p><p style=3D=
"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Some=
 Yemenis on the ground call them the =E2=80=9Chotel government=E2=80=9D bec=
ause they basically live in hotels in Riyadh and they have, you know, not a=
 whole lot of credibility. They=E2=80=99re beholden to Saudi Arabia, which =
spent years bombing Yemen and is not popular there.</span></p><p style=3D"f=
ont:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>So the=
 Houthis now describe themselves as the state of Yemen. Yes, they=E2=80=99r=
e a pariah group, they=E2=80=99re under sanctions and we refer to them as a=
 militia. Humanitarian conditions in northern Yemen, which they control, ar=
e desperate. But they do provide relative security in their territory under=
 one unified authority, which many Yemenis complain that the Yemeni governm=
ent does not. The economic situation is also not much better in government =
territory.</span></p><table border=3D"0" cellpadding=3D"0" cellspacing=3D"0=
